Here are the standard **RTSP client request templates** (excluding the `DESCRIBE` example you already provided):

```
OPTIONS: ["OPTIONS <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
DESCRIBE: ["DESCRIBE <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","Accept: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
ANNOUNCE: ["ANNOUNCE <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","Content-Length: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
SETUP: ["SETUP <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","Transport: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
PLAY: ["PLAY <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","Range: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
PAUSE: ["PAUSE <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
TEARDOWN: ["TEARDOWN <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
GET_PARAMETER: ["GET_PARAMETER <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
SET_PARAMETER: ["SET_PARAMETER <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","Content-Length: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
REDIRECT: ["REDIRECT <<VALUE>>\r\n","CSeq: <<VALUE>>\r\n","User-Agent: <<VALUE>>\r\n","\r\n"]
```

**Note:**  
- `<<VALUE>>` placeholders should be replaced with actual values (URL, sequence numbers, transport parameters, etc.).  
- `CSeq` (Command Sequence) increments with each request.  
- `Transport` header is critical for `SETUP` to specify RTP/RTCP details.  
- `Range` header in `PLAY` specifies playback start/end time.  

This covers all standard RTSP 1.0/2.0 client request methods.
